      "comment": "As a noun <span lang=\"la\">māne</span> is mostly poetic and post-Augustan (Lewis &amp; Short); in prose it is the adverb, “in the morning”: <span lang=\"la\">multō māne</span>, very early; <span lang=\"la\">hodiē māne</span>, this morning. It takes no adjective except in such fixed phrases."
